=== (H,c3) vs (H,c3,P) discriminating power ===
n=4: P func of H? False ; P func of (H,c3)? False ; P adds beyond (H,c3)? True ; #(H,c3)=3 #(H,c3,P)=4
n=5: P func of H? False ; P func of (H,c3)? False ; P adds beyond (H,c3)? True ; #(H,c3)=8 #(H,c3,P)=15
n=6: P func of H? False ; P func of (H,c3)? False ; P adds beyond (H,c3)? True ; #(H,c3)=24 #(H,c3,P)=138

=== P relabeling-(in)variance (is P a graph invariant or embedding artifact?) ===
n=5: sample tournament P(convex order)=1 ; P over relabelings = [1, 3, 5]  (DEPENDS ON EMBEDDING -> NOT a graph invariant)
n=6: sample tournament P(convex order)=8 ; P over relabelings = [4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12]  (DEPENDS ON EMBEDDING -> NOT a graph invariant)